{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you tonight. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi… I’ve been feeling really sick. Nauseous, throwing up, and my back pain’s been worse. My blood sugar’s been really high too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. When did the high blood sugars start?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Two days ago. I wasn’t eating much because I felt off, but I kept taking my Lantus at night like usual."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And when did the vomiting start?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yesterday. I couldn’t keep anything down, so I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:39:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. Your blood sugar was 595 when you arrived, and we saw some ketones. That means you were in diabetic ketoacidosis. We gave you insulin and fluids in the ER to start correcting it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh… I didn’t realize it was that bad. I thought it was just another high sugar episode."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:41:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It was serious, but we’ve already started treatment. Your anion gap is closing, which means the acidosis is improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good… I hate feeling this way. It happens a lot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:43:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I know this isn’t the first time. We’re going to keep you NPO for now—no food or drink by mouth—for the next few hours to let your stomach settle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:44:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Will I get something for the nausea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve given you Reglan and ondansetron through your IV. You should start feeling better soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. What about my back pain? It’s been really bothering me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked your back—no tenderness. It might be related to your high sugars or muscle tension. We gave you dilaudid earlier, and we can continue with pain meds as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that helps. I’ve had back pain since my car accident years ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see that in your history. You’re on gabapentin—still helping?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:50:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, it helps some. I also use the lidocaine patch."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:51:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep that up. We also did a CT scan of your abdomen and pelvis to make sure there’s nothing else going on."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:52:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Was there anything wrong?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:53:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The scan was clear—no abscess, no blockage. Your liver and pancreas look normal too. That’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:54:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried it might be my stomach again—like the gastroparesis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:55:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We know you’ve had that diagnosis, but your recent gastric emptying study was normal. Still, high sugars can make nausea worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:56:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I just don’t always know what triggers the highs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:57:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll work with the endocrinology team to adjust your insulin. They recommend lowering your Lantus dose to 24 units at bedtime."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:58:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "From 28? Why is that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2125-07-28 23:59:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Because we want to avoid lows, especially since you’re not eating. We’ll also give you a tighter sliding scale for your Humalog."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2125-07-29 00:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I can follow that. I’ve messed up before by overcorrecting at night."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2125-07-29 00:01:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we saw that in your last admission. It’s important to balance correction without going too low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2125-07-29 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood sugar last night dropped to 230 and stayed in the 200s. This morning it’s 179—much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2125-07-29 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Can I eat something now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2125-07-29 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re going to start you on clear liquids and slowly advance to a regular diet. We’ll watch how you tolerate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2125-07-29 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I’m really hungry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2125-07-29 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well with the clear liquids. We’re upgrading you to a regular diet for lunch."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2125-07-29 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. No nausea so far."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2125-07-29 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. Your kidney function was a little off on admission—creatinine was 1.5—but it’s improving with fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2125-07-29 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that from dehydration?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2125-07-29 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and possibly from your lisinopril. We held it temporarily, but we’ll restart it today since your levels are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2125-07-29 12:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I know I need to drink more water."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2125-07-30 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done really well. Your blood sugars are stable—no highs or lows—and you’ve kept your meals down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2125-07-30 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2125-07-30 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re discharging you today. We’ve updated your insulin: 24 units of glargine at bedtime and a new sliding scale for your aspart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2125-07-30 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll need to review the sheet carefully."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2125-07-30 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Absolutely. We’ve also set up follow-up with your PCP, a counselor through social work, and GI for your esophageal varices."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2125-07-30 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve missed some appointments before… but I want to do better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2125-07-30 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a great step. Your team is here to support you. Keep using your nausea med as needed, and monitor your sugars closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2125-07-30 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thank you for helping me through this again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2125-07-30 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and call your doctor if you start feeling unwell again."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2125-07-28 23:33:00",
    "admission_end": "2125-07-30 14:59:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type 1 diabetes and a history of frequent hospitalizations for nausea, vomiting, and back pain was admitted with diabetic ketoacidosis due to uncontrolled hyperglycemia. She presented with high blood glucose of 595, an elevated anion gap, and dehydration. She was treated with IV fluids and insulin, which resolved the acidosis. Her diet was advanced successfully, and her blood sugars stabilized. Imaging showed no acute abdominal process. Her insulin regimen was adjusted to 24 units of glargine at bedtime with a revised sliding scale. Acute kidney injury improved with hydration, and lisinopril was restarted. Social work facilitated outpatient mental health and medical follow-up to address ongoing challenges with adherence and anxiety. She was discharged home in stable condition with updated medications and coordinated follow-up care.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with ketoacidosis, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Diabetes with renal manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Esophageal varices without mention of bleeding",
      "Diabetes with other specified manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Dehydration",
      "Dysthymic disorder",
      "Nephritis and nephropathy, not specified as acute or chronic, in diseases classified elsewhere",
      "Lumbago",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Other and unspecified hyperlipidemia",
      "Goiter, unspecified",
      "Personal history of noncompliance with medical treatment, presenting hazards to health",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin"
    ]
  }
}
